   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 45,
   "message": "A diverged bundle is documented as kept (`resume_bundle` warns, `drop_bundle` keeps it), but `save_bundle` still overwrites the pair unconditionally. If the next push also fails, `work.base` and `work.bundle` are replaced by a bundle of `BUNDLE_BASE..branch` built from the remote-based branch. The only copy of the diverged commits is destroyed. Fix: before replacing the pair, check that the existing bundle's tips are contained in the new branch, as `drop_bundle` does. If they are not, keep the old pair or write under a different name, and record that in `bundle=`.",
   "original_severity": "major",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B12",
   "scenario": "Run 1 push fails, so a bundle holds commits X. The remote change branch then moves to Y, diverged from X. Run 2 resumes the remote branch, warns 'diverged ... keeping the bundle', and its push fails too. `save_bundle` runs `bundle create work.bundle.tmp BUNDLE_BASE..refs/heads/b` on the Y-based branch and renames it over `work.bundle`, so X is gone and the record says `bundle=saved`.",
   "severity": "major",
   "unclassified": false
  }
 ],
